# 1. System: an adaptive research agent with durable evidence

[Package home](../README.md) · [Next: capsules](02-capsules.md)

**The agent owns an evolving investigation; the runtime owns permission to execute and authority to accept results.** JiuwenSwarm reasons, delegates, schedules existing jobs and manages agent sessions. AI4R adds research contracts, portable capsules, checked calls and durable evidence. These are responsibilities, not a requirement for one new service per box.

![System ownership](../diagrams/01-system.svg)

| Owner | Responsibility | Cannot decide alone |
|---|---|---|
| Human / project policy | Research objective, constraints, budgets, disclosure permissions, consequential changes | Whether an unsupported scientific claim is true |
| Intent capability | Clarify who wants what and preserve uncertainties | Invent answers to missing requirements |
| Contract capability + protected binder | Turn the objective into versioned acceptance obligations; bind permitted checks and effects before work | Let a producer edit its own success criteria |
| JiuwenSwarm agent | Revise agenda, select capabilities, delegate, compare evidence, request clarification | Bypass mandatory checks, expand permissions or promote a release |
| Capsule runtime | Validate input, pin calls, enforce checks/budgets, produce receipts | Treat a model's confident prose as proof |
| Existing execution/session providers | Run, cancel, checkpoint and reconcile work within enforced limits | Report a timed-out thread as certainly stopped |
| Evidence/artifact store | Preserve sources, lineage, call status, exact bytes and publication manifest | Silently replace accepted artifacts |
| Admission/quality policy | Qualify releases and environments; reevaluate use evidence | Select the research question or rewrite project history |

## A concrete long-running flow

![Changing the next experiment](../diagrams/02-research-flow.svg)

A researcher asks whether a workload predictor generalizes to a new hardware family. The agent clarifies “generalizes,” binds a held-out test and resource limit, obtains traces and a baseline, then runs a checked experiment. A result reveals data leakage: affected metrics are invalidated, the agent changes preprocessing and reruns the affected work. The negative observation and earlier artifacts remain visible. A new library released next week becomes a candidate, is qualified, and can be selected for a new experiment. Existing results keep their original environment pins. Comparing versions is a new controlled comparison, not retroactive replacement.

Plan only as far as useful given present uncertainty. Reconsider after a result, failure, changed assumption, new capability, budget boundary or human correction. The future agenda is editable. A dispatched call and a preregistered experiment's criteria are immutable; changing either creates a new revision/attempt with the reason and affected evidence recorded.

## What it supports

Research literature, data preparation, code and program construction, asynchronous benchmarks, analysis, reports, bounded specialist agents, human questions and qualified new capabilities all use the same call/evidence rules. Existing deterministic workflows may be invoked as one capability or a recipe. They are not the global control structure.

The agent may use native reasoning and ordinary low-risk support operations without a CC. Any operation producing accepted research evidence or external effects must cross the declared provider/check boundary, whether implemented by a CC or a governed native tool. An unrestricted native tool must not become a bypass. No tool pool can make an ungrounded conclusion reliable by itself.

**Acceptance:** a late discovery changes the next experiment without restarting valid work, changing past criteria or losing provenance. See M2A-01, 04, 08 and 12 in the [acceptance matrix](../3-agent-reference/acceptance-matrix.json).
